  "chapter": 834,
  "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
  "text": " \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 170 Chapter 834\n \n       MEMORANDUM filed with Assembly Bill Number 3130, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT to amend the executive law, in relation to establishing the\n        office of the advocate for people with disabilities\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This bill would enshrine in statute an advocate for people with  disa-\nbilities.  In  1983,  the  \"State  Office  of Advocate for the Disabled\"\n(Office) was established through Executive Order 26. The primary task of\nthis Office was to advocate on behalf of persons with  disabilities  and\nimplement laws that prevent discrimination against persons with disabil-\nities.  However,  the  function  of  this  Office  was to a large extent\nsubsumed into a different body when the Commission on  Quality  of  Care\nand  Advocacy  for  Persons  with  Disabilities (CQC) was established in\n2011. The CQC was  then  disbanded  when  the  Justice  Center  for  the\nProtection  of  People  with  Special  Needs  (The  Justice  Center) was\ncreated.\n \n  While there have been many advances  in  the  services  available  for\npeople  with disabilities, it is critical to prioritize the needs of the\nentire disability community, which includes individuals  with  physical,\nsensory, mobility, intellectual, developmental, and psychiatric disabil-\nities, with a Chief Disability Officer.\n \n  I  strongly  support  the  intent  of  this bill and I have reached an\nagreement with the Legislature to make technical changes to the bill  to\nensure  that  the  Chief Disability Officer will function as an advocate\nfor the rights of all people with disabilities and will ensure that such\nindividuals can exercise all the rights accorded  to  citizens  of  this\nstate.\n\n  The bill is approved.                          (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2021
 },
